1
00:00:02,522 --> 00:00:03,647
Water.

2
00:00:04,941 --> 00:00:06,316
Earth.

3
00:00:06,859 --> 00:00:08,402
Fire.

4
00:00:09,028 --> 00:00:10,320
Air.

5
00:00:11,239 --> 00:00:14,616
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:19,246
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,706 --> 00:00:22,582
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:23,750
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,835 --> 00:00:26,628
But when the world
needed him most, he vanished.

10
00:00:27,422 --> 00:00:28,463
100 years passed,

11
00:00:28,548 --> 00:00:31,258
and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

12
00:00:31,342 --> 00:00:32,843
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:33,136 --> 00:00:35,220
And although
his airbending skills are great,

14
00:00:35,305 --> 00:00:38,473
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone,

15
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:42,102
But I believe Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:56,367 --> 00:00:57,367
Look!

17
00:01:04,292 --> 00:01:05,667
He is taunting us.

18
00:01:06,753 --> 00:01:08,211
You are so going to be dinner.

19
00:01:10,631 --> 00:01:12,716
Hey, where's the fishing line?

20
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:15,302
I didn't think
you would need it, Sokka.

21
00:01:16,304 --> 00:01:17,846
It's all tangled.

22
00:01:18,681 --> 00:01:20,432
Not tangled, woven.

23
00:01:20,516 --> 00:01:22,184
I made you a necklace, Katara.

24
00:01:22,769 --> 00:01:24,895
I thought since you lost
your other one...

25
00:01:28,191 --> 00:01:29,191
Thanks, Aang.

26
00:01:29,275 --> 00:01:30,275
I love it.

27
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:31,693
Great, Aang.

28
00:01:31,778 --> 00:01:33,278
Maybe instead of saving the world,

29
00:01:33,363 --> 00:01:34,988
you can go
into the jewelry-making business.

30
00:01:35,531 --> 00:01:37,115
I don't see why I can't do both.

31
00:01:40,787 --> 00:01:42,079
Stop taunting me!

32
00:01:45,958 --> 00:01:47,376
So, how do I look?

33
00:01:53,091 --> 00:01:55,300
You mean, all of you
or just your neck--

34
00:01:55,385 --> 00:01:57,219
I mean, because they both look great.

35
00:01:57,595 --> 00:01:58,929
Smoochie smoochie.

36
00:01:59,222 --> 00:02:01,473
Someone's in love.

37
00:02:02,141 --> 00:02:03,767
I, well--

38
00:02:04,268 --> 00:02:05,644
Stop teasing him, Sokka.

39
00:02:05,978 --> 00:02:07,479
Aang's just a good friend,

40
00:02:07,563 --> 00:02:10,357
a sweet little guy, just like Momo.

41
00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:11,650
Thanks.

42
00:02:17,448 --> 00:02:19,408
Someone's being attacked
by a platypus bear!

43
00:02:32,046 --> 00:02:33,088
Well, hello there.

44
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,382
Nice day, isn't it?

45
00:02:35,550 --> 00:02:37,008
Make noise! He'll run off!

46
00:02:37,093 --> 00:02:38,969
No, play dead! He'll lose interest!

47
00:02:39,554 --> 00:02:42,347
Whoa, close one. Ha ha ha.

48
00:02:43,099 --> 00:02:44,766
Run downhill, then climb a tree!

49
00:02:44,851 --> 00:02:46,351
No, punch him in the bill!

50
00:02:46,436 --> 00:02:47,894
And then run in zig-zags.

51
00:02:48,646 --> 00:02:49,729
No need.

52
00:02:49,814 --> 00:02:51,106
It's going to be fine.

53
00:02:58,531 --> 00:02:59,531
Whoa, there.

54
00:03:09,542 --> 00:03:11,209
Lunch.

55
00:03:12,503 --> 00:03:14,296
Lucky for you we came along.

56
00:03:14,505 --> 00:03:17,966
Thanks, but everything
was already under control.

57
00:03:18,426 --> 00:03:19,801
Not to worry.

58
00:03:19,886 --> 00:03:22,804
Aunt Wu predicted
I'd have a safe journey.

59
00:03:23,181 --> 00:03:24,181
Aunt who?

60
00:03:24,265 --> 00:03:25,849
No, Aunt Wu.

61
00:03:25,933 --> 00:03:28,560
She's the fortune-teller
from my village.

62
00:03:29,353 --> 00:03:31,313
Awful nice knowing your future.

63
00:03:31,397 --> 00:03:33,315
Wow, it must be.

64
00:03:33,608 --> 00:03:35,358
That explains why you were so calm.

65
00:03:35,776 --> 00:03:37,736
But the fortune-teller was wrong.

66
00:03:37,862 --> 00:03:39,070
You didn't have a safe journey.

67
00:03:39,155 --> 00:03:40,197
You were almost killed.

68
00:03:40,865 --> 00:03:42,032
But I wasn't.

69
00:03:42,116 --> 00:03:43,909
All right, have a good one.

70
00:03:46,496 --> 00:03:50,415
And Aunt Wu said if I met
any travelers, to give them this.

71
00:03:54,670 --> 00:03:57,047
Maybe we should go see Aunt Wu
and learn our fortunes.

72
00:03:57,131 --> 00:03:58,423
It could be fun.

73
00:03:58,508 --> 00:04:01,384
Come on.
Fortune-telling is nonsense.

74
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:03,470
What do you know?

75
00:04:03,554 --> 00:04:04,554
An umbrella.

76
00:04:06,974 --> 00:04:07,974
That proves it.

77
00:04:08,059 --> 00:04:09,226
No, it doesn't.

78
00:04:09,644 --> 00:04:11,728
You can't really tell the future.

79
00:04:11,812 --> 00:04:14,231
I guess you're not
really getting wet, then.

80
00:04:14,774 --> 00:04:17,526
Whoa-- Aah!

81
00:04:17,944 --> 00:04:18,944
Of course she predicted

82
00:04:19,028 --> 00:04:20,028
it was gonna rain.

83
00:04:20,112 --> 00:04:21,446
The sky has been grey all day.

84
00:04:21,531 --> 00:04:23,281
Just admit you might be wrong,

85
00:04:23,366 --> 00:04:24,741
and you can come under the umbrella.

86
00:04:25,785 --> 00:04:27,577
Look, I'm gonna
predict the future now.

87
00:04:27,662 --> 00:04:30,497
It's going to keep drizzling.

88
00:04:31,958 --> 00:04:33,250
See?

89
00:04:34,961 --> 00:04:36,753
Not everyone has the gift, Sokka.

90
00:04:40,383 --> 00:04:41,383
Aah!

91
00:04:56,524 --> 00:04:59,276
Aunt Wu is expecting you.

92
00:04:59,652 --> 00:05:00,944
Really?

93
00:05:01,028 --> 00:05:02,112
Pfft.

94
00:05:06,492 --> 00:05:10,078
My name is Meng,
and I'm Aunt Wu's assistant.

95
00:05:15,334 --> 00:05:16,793
Well, hello there.

96
00:05:18,212 --> 00:05:19,254
Hello.

97
00:05:19,338 --> 00:05:20,672
Can I get you some tea

98
00:05:20,756 --> 00:05:23,174
or some of Aunt Wu's
special bean curd puffs?

99
00:05:23,634 --> 00:05:24,634
I'll try a curd puff.

100
00:05:24,719 --> 00:05:25,719
Just a second.

101
00:05:26,137 --> 00:05:27,137
So, what's your name?

102
00:05:27,221 --> 00:05:28,221
Aang.

103
00:05:28,806 --> 00:05:30,599
That rhymes with Meng,

104
00:05:30,683 --> 00:05:33,476
and you've got some pretty big ears,
don't you?

105
00:05:34,478 --> 00:05:35,937
I guess.

106
00:05:36,355 --> 00:05:37,564
Don't be modest.

107
00:05:37,648 --> 00:05:38,648
They're huge.

108
00:05:38,983 --> 00:05:41,443
Well, Aang, it's very nice
to meet you--

109
00:05:41,902 --> 00:05:43,069
Very nice.

110
00:05:43,154 --> 00:05:44,446
Likewise.

111
00:05:45,364 --> 00:05:46,656
I can't believe we're here

112
00:05:46,741 --> 00:05:47,949
in the house of nonsense.

113
00:05:48,367 --> 00:05:50,577
Try to keep an open mind, Sokka.

114
00:05:50,661 --> 00:05:51,828
There are things in this world

115
00:05:51,912 --> 00:05:53,330
that just can't be explained.

116
00:05:53,414 --> 00:05:55,999
Wouldn't it be nice to have
some insight into your future?

117
00:05:56,083 --> 00:05:58,501
It would be nice
to have some bean curd puffs.

118
00:06:00,546 --> 00:06:02,047
Meng!

119
00:06:02,131 --> 00:06:04,924
Aunt Wu says
I'm going to meet my true love!

120
00:06:05,343 --> 00:06:08,178
He's going to give me
a rare panda lily.

121
00:06:08,471 --> 00:06:10,889
That's so romantic.

122
00:06:11,474 --> 00:06:14,976
I wonder if my true love
will give me a rare flower.

123
00:06:15,061 --> 00:06:16,353
Good luck with that.

124
00:06:17,605 --> 00:06:20,899
Is that the big-eared guy
who Aunt Wu predicted you'd marry?

125
00:06:24,862 --> 00:06:25,862
Aah!

126
00:06:29,575 --> 00:06:30,825
Enjoy your snack.

127
00:06:33,204 --> 00:06:35,455
Welcome, young travelers.

128
00:06:35,539 --> 00:06:36,665
Now, who's next?

129
00:06:37,291 --> 00:06:38,917
Don't be shy.

130
00:06:42,213 --> 00:06:43,672
I guess that's me.

131
00:06:44,924 --> 00:06:46,883
Not bad, not bad.

132
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,138
I'm good on puffs.

133
00:06:54,225 --> 00:06:57,727
So, what do you think
they're talking about back there?

134
00:06:57,812 --> 00:06:59,270
Boring stuff, I'm sure.

135
00:06:59,355 --> 00:07:00,939
Love, who she's gonna marry,

136
00:07:01,023 --> 00:07:02,732
how many babies she's gonna have.

137
00:07:02,817 --> 00:07:05,235
Yeah, dumb stuff like that.

138
00:07:05,861 --> 00:07:07,404
Well, I gotta find a bathroom.

139
00:07:12,576 --> 00:07:14,494
Your palms are so smooth.

140
00:07:14,578 --> 00:07:16,913
Do you use moisturizer?

141
00:07:16,997 --> 00:07:19,791
Actually,
I have this special seaweed lotion.

142
00:07:20,042 --> 00:07:22,210
I could get you some if you want.

143
00:07:22,294 --> 00:07:25,547
So, do you see anything
interesting in my love line?

144
00:07:25,631 --> 00:07:28,216
I see a great romance for you--

145
00:07:28,801 --> 00:07:30,301
The man you're going to marry.

146
00:07:30,386 --> 00:07:31,720
Tell me more!

147
00:07:31,804 --> 00:07:35,849
I can see
that he's a very powerful bender.

148
00:07:43,733 --> 00:07:46,025
Looks like someone
had a pretty good bathroom break.

149
00:07:46,861 --> 00:07:48,486
Yeah, when I was in there--

150
00:07:48,571 --> 00:07:49,738
I don't even want to know.

151
00:07:49,822 --> 00:07:50,989
Who's next?

152
00:07:51,073 --> 00:07:53,116
Ok, let's get this over with.

153
00:07:53,451 --> 00:07:56,703
Your future is full
of struggle and anguish,

154
00:07:56,787 --> 00:07:59,664
most of it self-inflicted.

155
00:08:00,124 --> 00:08:02,041
But you didn't read
my palms or anything.

156
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:03,752
I don't need to.

157
00:08:03,836 --> 00:08:05,545
It's written all over your face.

158
00:08:08,549 --> 00:08:11,050
You there, come with me.

159
00:08:13,137 --> 00:08:16,473
This is the most reliable method
of telling your fortune.

160
00:08:16,932 --> 00:08:18,516
The bones never lie.

161
00:08:19,059 --> 00:08:20,769
Go on. Pick one.

162
00:08:22,897 --> 00:08:24,647
Now throw it on the fire.

163
00:08:25,608 --> 00:08:28,026
The heat makes cracks in the bones,

164
00:08:28,444 --> 00:08:31,696
and I read the bone cracks
to tell your destiny.

165
00:08:33,157 --> 00:08:35,074
Wow, that's a big crack.

166
00:08:36,619 --> 00:08:38,286
I've never seen this before.

167
00:08:41,999 --> 00:08:43,166
My!

168
00:08:49,924 --> 00:08:52,717
Your destiny-- This is incredible.

169
00:08:52,802 --> 00:08:56,513
You will be involved
in a great battle--

170
00:08:56,597 --> 00:09:00,391
An awesome conflict
between the forces of good and evil.

171
00:09:00,476 --> 00:09:05,063
A battle whose outcome will determine
the fate of the whole world.

172
00:09:05,314 --> 00:09:07,148
Yeah, yeah. I knew that already,

173
00:09:07,233 --> 00:09:08,817
But did it say anything about a girl?

174
00:09:09,193 --> 00:09:10,235
A girl?

175
00:09:10,319 --> 00:09:11,986
You want to know about love?

176
00:09:12,071 --> 00:09:13,196
Yes!

177
00:09:13,906 --> 00:09:15,615
I'm sorry, but I didn't see anything.

178
00:09:18,369 --> 00:09:19,577
Look!

179
00:09:19,662 --> 00:09:21,371
I must have missed something.

180
00:09:21,872 --> 00:09:23,122
Right here.

181
00:09:23,207 --> 00:09:28,336
It says, "trust your heart, and you
will be with the one you love."

182
00:09:28,671 --> 00:09:29,838
Really?

183
00:09:29,922 --> 00:09:31,089
Thank you, Aunt Wu!

184
00:09:34,093 --> 00:09:35,718
Well, now you got to see
for yourselves

185
00:09:35,803 --> 00:09:38,221
that fortune-telling
is just a big, stupid hoax.

186
00:09:38,472 --> 00:09:39,681
You're just saying that

187
00:09:39,765 --> 00:09:41,850
because you're gonna make yourself
unhappy your whole life.

188
00:09:41,934 --> 00:09:43,560
That woman is crazy!

189
00:09:44,019 --> 00:09:47,605
My life will be calm and happy
and joyful!

190
00:09:50,651 --> 00:09:52,318
That doesn't prove anything.

191
00:09:52,403 --> 00:09:54,279
Well, I liked my predictions.

192
00:09:54,697 --> 00:09:57,156
Certain things
are gonna turn out very well.

193
00:09:57,408 --> 00:09:58,950
They sure are.

194
00:09:59,034 --> 00:10:00,118
Why?

195
00:10:00,202 --> 00:10:01,202
What did she tell you?

196
00:10:01,662 --> 00:10:02,662
Some stuff.

197
00:10:02,746 --> 00:10:03,746
You'll find out.

198
00:10:09,295 --> 00:10:10,461
What's with the sky?

199
00:10:10,921 --> 00:10:13,506
We're waiting for Aunt Wu
to come and read the clouds

200
00:10:13,591 --> 00:10:15,508
to predict the fate
of the whole village.

201
00:10:15,593 --> 00:10:17,760
That cloud kind of looks
like a fluffy bunny.

202
00:10:18,304 --> 00:10:20,346
You better hope that's not a bunny.

203
00:10:20,431 --> 00:10:23,474
The fluffy bunny cloud
forecasts doom and destruction.

204
00:10:23,851 --> 00:10:25,476
Do you even hear yourself?

205
00:10:25,978 --> 00:10:27,979
The cloud reading
will tell us if Mount Makapu

206
00:10:28,063 --> 00:10:30,148
will remain dormant for another year

207
00:10:30,232 --> 00:10:31,232
or if it will erupt.

208
00:10:31,734 --> 00:10:33,860
We used to have
a tradition once a year

209
00:10:33,944 --> 00:10:35,111
of going up the mountain

210
00:10:35,195 --> 00:10:36,863
to check the volcano ourselves,

211
00:10:37,281 --> 00:10:38,907
But ever since Aunt Wu

212
00:10:38,991 --> 00:10:40,992
moved to the village 20 years ago,

213
00:10:41,076 --> 00:10:44,203
we have a tradition of not doing that.

214
00:10:44,538 --> 00:10:46,539
I can't believe
you would trust your lives

215
00:10:46,624 --> 00:10:48,708
to that crazy
old woman's superstition!

216
00:10:49,293 --> 00:10:50,835
Shh! She's coming.

217
00:10:54,924 --> 00:10:56,341
Hey, Aang,

218
00:10:56,425 --> 00:10:59,594
don't you think that cloud
looks like a flower?

219
00:11:00,304 --> 00:11:02,180
Sure, I guess.

220
00:11:02,890 --> 00:11:05,433
Hey, Katara, don't you think
that cloud looks like a flower?

221
00:11:05,517 --> 00:11:06,559
Shh!

222
00:11:13,275 --> 00:11:15,443
Bending arrow cloud--

223
00:11:15,527 --> 00:11:19,072
Good crops this year.
Nice, big harvest.

224
00:11:19,406 --> 00:11:21,449
Darn good news!

225
00:11:21,867 --> 00:11:25,453
Wavy moon-shaped cloud-- Let's see.

226
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:28,915
Gonna be a great year for twins.

227
00:11:29,249 --> 00:11:30,333
-Yes!
-Yes!

228
00:11:31,001 --> 00:11:35,171
And a cumulus cloud with a twisty
nub coming off the end of it--

229
00:11:35,756 --> 00:11:40,259
The village will not be destroyed
by the volcano this year!

230
00:11:42,346 --> 00:11:43,972
Since I got you here,

231
00:11:44,056 --> 00:11:46,140
there's something I want to tell you.

232
00:11:46,308 --> 00:11:48,476
I like you, but more than normal.

233
00:11:50,854 --> 00:11:51,854
Never mind.

234
00:11:58,737 --> 00:11:59,862
Hi, Aunt Wu.

235
00:11:59,947 --> 00:12:01,072
Sorry to bother you.

236
00:12:01,156 --> 00:12:02,281
Anytime.

237
00:12:02,366 --> 00:12:04,325
About this man I'm supposed to marry--

238
00:12:04,410 --> 00:12:05,618
Is he gonna be handsome?

239
00:12:05,703 --> 00:12:06,911
I hope he's tall.

240
00:12:07,538 --> 00:12:10,415
You want another reading.

241
00:12:10,624 --> 00:12:11,624
Yes, please.

242
00:12:14,712 --> 00:12:16,546
I can't believe all these saps.

243
00:12:16,964 --> 00:12:19,215
Someone really needs
to scream some sense at them.

244
00:12:19,591 --> 00:12:21,259
They seem happy, Sokka.

245
00:12:21,343 --> 00:12:22,677
Not for long.

246
00:12:22,761 --> 00:12:25,179
I'm gonna prove
Aunt Wu's predictions are nonsense.

247
00:12:26,098 --> 00:12:27,140
Hey, you,

248
00:12:27,224 --> 00:12:29,934
I bet Aunt Wu told you to wear
those red shoes, didn't she?

249
00:12:30,019 --> 00:12:32,311
Yeah, she said
I'd be wearing red shoes

250
00:12:32,396 --> 00:12:33,646
when I met my true love.

251
00:12:35,107 --> 00:12:36,607
And how many times
have you worn those shoes

252
00:12:36,692 --> 00:12:37,942
since you got that fortune?

253
00:12:38,027 --> 00:12:39,277
Every day.

254
00:12:40,195 --> 00:12:42,530
Then of course it's gonna come true!

255
00:12:43,073 --> 00:12:44,741
Really? You think so?

256
00:12:44,825 --> 00:12:46,576
I'm so excited!

257
00:12:49,496 --> 00:12:52,206
Aah! Uhh!

258
00:12:53,083 --> 00:12:55,585
And then you'll have
your third great grandchild

259
00:12:55,669 --> 00:12:58,713
before quietly
passing away in your sleep.

260
00:12:58,797 --> 00:13:00,423
Is that enough information for you?

261
00:13:00,883 --> 00:13:03,509
Wow. Thanks, Aunt Wu.

262
00:13:03,594 --> 00:13:05,428
Wait. One more thing.

263
00:13:05,888 --> 00:13:08,097
How warmly should I dress tomorrow?

264
00:13:08,432 --> 00:13:10,433
You want me to do a reading for that?

265
00:13:12,102 --> 00:13:14,395
I don't care what Aunt Wu told you!

266
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:16,814
You have to take a bath sometime!

267
00:13:20,903 --> 00:13:23,863
So, Sokka, you know some stuff
about ladies, right?

268
00:13:23,947 --> 00:13:25,114
Some stuff?

269
00:13:25,199 --> 00:13:26,908
You've come to the right place.

270
00:13:26,992 --> 00:13:28,409
What can I do you for?

271
00:13:28,827 --> 00:13:30,286
Well, there's this girl...

272
00:13:32,456 --> 00:13:34,332
I think I know who you mean.

273
00:13:34,666 --> 00:13:36,501
You do? And you're ok with it?

274
00:13:36,585 --> 00:13:37,919
Of course I am.

275
00:13:38,003 --> 00:13:39,295
And to tell you the truth,

276
00:13:39,379 --> 00:13:41,339
I've been picking up
a subtle vibe that she likes you, too.

277
00:13:41,507 --> 00:13:42,507
She does?

278
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:44,801
Yeah. She's crazy about you.

279
00:13:44,885 --> 00:13:47,053
All you have to do now
is not mess it up.

280
00:13:47,471 --> 00:13:48,971
Well, how do I do that?

281
00:13:49,056 --> 00:13:51,224
The number one mistake
nice guys like you make--

282
00:13:51,308 --> 00:13:52,767
Being too nice.

283
00:13:53,227 --> 00:13:54,811
You can be too nice?

284
00:13:54,895 --> 00:13:57,188
Yep. If you want to
keep her interested,

285
00:13:57,272 --> 00:13:58,731
you have to act aloof,

286
00:13:59,108 --> 00:14:00,900
Like you don't really care
one way or the other.

287
00:14:01,235 --> 00:14:03,361
Well, ok.

288
00:14:03,445 --> 00:14:05,863
Hey, Aang. I was wondering--

289
00:14:05,948 --> 00:14:07,240
See you later.

290
00:14:08,992 --> 00:14:11,577
Wow. That kid is good.

291
00:14:12,371 --> 00:14:14,747
And you'll be fine
as long as you've got a scarf.

292
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,207
Bye-bye, now.

293
00:14:16,542 --> 00:14:18,918
Ok, ok. But one more thing.

294
00:14:19,211 --> 00:14:21,254
All right. What is it?

295
00:14:21,547 --> 00:14:24,841
Should I eat a mango or a papaya

296
00:14:24,925 --> 00:14:26,092
for breakfast tomorrow?

297
00:14:26,176 --> 00:14:27,593
Papaya.

298
00:14:28,262 --> 00:14:30,263
I hate papaya.

299
00:14:30,514 --> 00:14:32,348
Hey, Katara.

300
00:14:32,432 --> 00:14:33,516
I didn't see you there.

301
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,226
Hey, Aang.

302
00:14:35,561 --> 00:14:36,727
That's ok.

303
00:14:36,812 --> 00:14:38,229
I'm busy with my own stuff.

304
00:14:46,905 --> 00:14:48,656
Papaya, please.

305
00:14:49,867 --> 00:14:51,826
So, papaya.

306
00:14:51,910 --> 00:14:54,036
Would you like some?

307
00:14:54,246 --> 00:14:55,371
You know me.

308
00:14:55,455 --> 00:14:57,123
I don't really care what I eat.

309
00:14:57,749 --> 00:14:58,749
Ok, then.

310
00:14:58,834 --> 00:14:59,876
See you later.

311
00:15:02,171 --> 00:15:03,838
Maybe aloof isn't my style.

312
00:15:04,173 --> 00:15:06,674
A panda lily.

313
00:15:07,968 --> 00:15:09,260
Did you see that?

314
00:15:10,846 --> 00:15:13,806
Excuse me. Where can a guy
find one of those things?

315
00:15:15,350 --> 00:15:17,476
I can't believe you're
dragging me all the way up here

316
00:15:17,561 --> 00:15:19,061
For a stupid flower.

317
00:15:19,146 --> 00:15:22,064
Not just any flower-- A panda lily.

318
00:15:22,274 --> 00:15:24,650
I've seen it in action,
and, boy, does it work.

319
00:15:25,527 --> 00:15:27,612
Flowers are fine once you're married,

320
00:15:27,696 --> 00:15:29,238
but at this early stage,

321
00:15:29,323 --> 00:15:32,366
it's critical that you maintain
maximum aloofness.

322
00:15:33,493 --> 00:15:35,119
But my heart
is telling me to get this flower,

323
00:15:35,370 --> 00:15:37,371
And Aunt Wu said
if I trusted my heart,

324
00:15:37,456 --> 00:15:38,998
I would be with the one I love.

325
00:15:39,499 --> 00:15:42,752
What? Don't tell me
you believe in that stuff, too.

326
00:15:43,378 --> 00:15:46,047
Well, Aunt Wu hasn't been wrong yet.

327
00:15:46,131 --> 00:15:47,673
Why should she be wrong about love?

328
00:15:50,302 --> 00:15:51,552
There, on the rim!

329
00:15:57,059 --> 00:15:58,684
Oh, no.

330
00:15:59,228 --> 00:16:00,436
Aunt Wu was wrong.

331
00:16:12,532 --> 00:16:13,741
Those people all think they're safe.

332
00:16:13,825 --> 00:16:15,284
We've got to warn them.

333
00:16:15,619 --> 00:16:16,827
There's no time to walk.

334
00:16:17,079 --> 00:16:18,079
Grab on.

335
00:16:18,163 --> 00:16:19,288
Aah!

336
00:16:28,548 --> 00:16:29,840
Hi, Katara.

337
00:16:29,925 --> 00:16:31,926
Can you believe she won't let me in?

338
00:16:32,177 --> 00:16:33,636
And after all the business
I've given her?

339
00:16:33,929 --> 00:16:35,096
But she doesn't even charge.

340
00:16:35,597 --> 00:16:36,722
I know, but still.

341
00:16:37,182 --> 00:16:39,225
Well, we have other things
to worry about.

342
00:16:39,309 --> 00:16:41,269
Aunt Wu was wrong about the volcano.

343
00:16:41,603 --> 00:16:44,188
Sokka, you tried to convince me
she was wrong before.

344
00:16:44,273 --> 00:16:45,731
It's gonna take an awful lot
to change my--

345
00:16:47,943 --> 00:16:49,068
Oh, no.

346
00:16:50,362 --> 00:16:53,155
Everyone, that volcano
is gonna blow any second!

347
00:16:53,615 --> 00:16:55,449
Aunt Wu was wrong!

348
00:16:55,534 --> 00:16:58,494
Yeah, yeah. We know
you don't believe in Aunt Wu,

349
00:16:58,578 --> 00:17:00,204
Mr. Science and Reason lover.

350
00:17:00,622 --> 00:17:03,499
If you won't listen to him,
maybe you'll listen to me.

351
00:17:03,834 --> 00:17:06,460
I want to believe Aunt Wu and her
predictions as much as you do,

352
00:17:06,545 --> 00:17:08,754
but my brother and Aang saw the lava

353
00:17:08,839 --> 00:17:10,089
with their own eyes.

354
00:17:10,173 --> 00:17:14,844
Well, I heard Aunt Wu's prediction
with my own ears.

355
00:17:15,971 --> 00:17:17,305
Please listen to us!

356
00:17:17,389 --> 00:17:19,015
You are all in danger,

357
00:17:19,099 --> 00:17:21,058
and we have to get out of here!

358
00:17:21,143 --> 00:17:23,185
You can't rely
on Aunt Wu's predictions!

359
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:26,105
You have to take fate
into your own hands!

360
00:17:26,940 --> 00:17:27,940
Look!

361
00:17:28,025 --> 00:17:29,942
Can your fortune-telling explain that?

362
00:17:32,529 --> 00:17:35,573
Heh. Can your science
explain why it rains?

363
00:17:35,907 --> 00:17:38,242
Yes! Yes, it can!

364
00:17:42,831 --> 00:17:44,749
They just won't listen to reason.

365
00:17:44,958 --> 00:17:47,251
But they will listen to Aunt Wu.

366
00:17:47,461 --> 00:17:49,128
I know. That's the problem.

367
00:17:49,338 --> 00:17:51,714
Well, it's about to become
the solution.

368
00:17:51,798 --> 00:17:53,841
We're taking fate in our own hands.

369
00:17:54,134 --> 00:17:56,635
First, I need to borrow
Aunt Wu's cloud-reading book.

370
00:18:06,396 --> 00:18:07,772
Shh.

371
00:18:07,856 --> 00:18:10,191
We don't want anyone to hear us.

372
00:18:10,567 --> 00:18:13,778
Oh! Oh, I didn't see you there.

373
00:18:14,279 --> 00:18:15,780
You don't like me, do you?

374
00:18:16,114 --> 00:18:17,531
Of course I like you.

375
00:18:17,908 --> 00:18:19,658
But not the way I like you.

376
00:18:20,619 --> 00:18:22,870
Oh. I guess not.

377
00:18:23,330 --> 00:18:24,830
It's ok.

378
00:18:24,915 --> 00:18:27,583
It's just really hard
when you like someone,

379
00:18:27,667 --> 00:18:30,211
but they don't think of you that way.

380
00:18:30,420 --> 00:18:32,046
I know what you mean.

381
00:18:32,255 --> 00:18:33,714
She's beautiful, by the way.

382
00:18:34,925 --> 00:18:36,634
That water tribe girl.

383
00:18:36,718 --> 00:18:38,636
I can see why you like her so much.

384
00:18:39,262 --> 00:18:41,305
She's sweet, she's a bender,

385
00:18:41,390 --> 00:18:45,309
and her hair seems so manageable.

386
00:18:46,478 --> 00:18:47,686
Don't worry.

387
00:18:47,771 --> 00:18:49,105
You're gonna meet a great guy

388
00:18:49,189 --> 00:18:50,523
who's gonna completely fall for you.

389
00:18:50,607 --> 00:18:51,607
I know it.

390
00:18:51,691 --> 00:18:52,858
Thanks.

391
00:18:53,610 --> 00:18:54,610
Wait.

392
00:18:54,820 --> 00:18:55,945
Don't you want this?

393
00:18:56,947 --> 00:18:58,197
How did you know?

394
00:18:58,281 --> 00:19:00,783
I've kind of been stalking you. Heh.

395
00:19:01,618 --> 00:19:02,910
Thanks...

396
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:04,745
I guess.

397
00:19:07,541 --> 00:19:09,166
Clouds are made
of water and air,

398
00:19:09,709 --> 00:19:10,960
So between the two of us,

399
00:19:11,044 --> 00:19:13,546
we ought to be able to bend them
into any shape we want.

400
00:19:14,089 --> 00:19:17,007
I found it--
The symbol for volcanic doom.

401
00:19:44,119 --> 00:19:45,953
Aunt Wu, look!

402
00:19:46,663 --> 00:19:48,330
Something's happening in the clouds!

403
00:19:48,623 --> 00:19:49,915
That's very strange.

404
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,751
It shouldn't-- Oh, my!

405
00:20:01,011 --> 00:20:03,429
We could still save the village
if we act fast.

406
00:20:03,847 --> 00:20:05,181
Sokka has a plan.

407
00:20:05,265 --> 00:20:07,641
Lava is gonna flow
downhill to this spot.

408
00:20:07,726 --> 00:20:09,185
If we can dig a deep enough trench,

409
00:20:09,269 --> 00:20:11,187
we can channel all the lava
away from the village

410
00:20:11,271 --> 00:20:12,271
to the river.

411
00:20:12,355 --> 00:20:14,690
If any of you are earth benders,
come with me.

412
00:20:15,108 --> 00:20:16,108
I'm an earth bender!

413
00:20:16,193 --> 00:20:17,193
I'm not!

414
00:20:17,569 --> 00:20:19,028
Everybody else, grab a shovel.

415
00:20:20,489 --> 00:20:21,655
Come on! We've got to hurry.

416
00:20:41,218 --> 00:20:42,968
Dig faster! Dig faster!

417
00:20:47,682 --> 00:20:49,642
Everyone needs to evacuate!

418
00:20:49,726 --> 00:20:50,893
We'll come for you when it's safe!

419
00:21:20,215 --> 00:21:21,382
It's too much.

420
00:21:21,466 --> 00:21:22,550
It's gonna overflow!

421
00:21:22,634 --> 00:21:23,634
Aah!

422
00:21:37,732 --> 00:21:38,941
Aah!

423
00:21:56,668 --> 00:21:57,668
Man...

424
00:21:58,044 --> 00:22:00,921
Sometimes I forget
what a powerful bender that kid is.

425
00:22:01,006 --> 00:22:02,965
Wait, what did you just say?

426
00:22:03,049 --> 00:22:05,301
Nothing. Just that Aang
is one powerful bender.

427
00:22:09,973 --> 00:22:12,099
I suppose he is.

428
00:22:17,731 --> 00:22:20,316
By the way,
we kind of borrowed your book.

429
00:22:20,650 --> 00:22:23,110
So you messed with the clouds,
did you?

430
00:22:24,070 --> 00:22:27,197
Ha ha ha! Very clever.

431
00:22:27,616 --> 00:22:29,908
No offense, but I hope this
has taught everyone a lesson

432
00:22:29,993 --> 00:22:32,536
about not relying too much
on fortune-telling.

433
00:22:32,746 --> 00:22:35,414
But Aunt Wu predicted
the village wouldn't be destroyed,

434
00:22:35,498 --> 00:22:36,582
and it wasn't.

435
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:38,542
She was right, after all.

436
00:22:38,627 --> 00:22:40,336
I hate you.

437
00:22:40,420 --> 00:22:41,920
It's ok, Sokka.

438
00:22:42,005 --> 00:22:43,881
Everything's gonna be all right.

439
00:22:44,090 --> 00:22:45,341
Can I ask you something?

440
00:22:45,425 --> 00:22:47,217
Of course, honey.

441
00:22:47,302 --> 00:22:49,678
You didn't really see love
in my fortune, did you?

442
00:22:49,763 --> 00:22:51,722
You just told me
what I wanted to hear.

443
00:22:52,015 --> 00:22:54,391
I'll tell you a little secret,
young airbender.

444
00:22:54,809 --> 00:22:57,394
Just as you reshaped those clouds,

445
00:22:57,646 --> 00:23:00,981
you have the power
to shape your own destiny.

446
00:23:02,150 --> 00:23:03,317
Good-bye, everyone!

447
00:23:03,401 --> 00:23:05,152
It was so nice to meet you!

448
00:23:05,654 --> 00:23:06,987
Take care, Meng.

449
00:23:07,072 --> 00:23:08,238
Take care!

450
00:23:12,786 --> 00:23:13,911
Floozy.
